			<div class="content" id="post-content-3584412">
									

<p>Seconding bittermixin's critisism of the final portion. After the slow buildup, probing at the edges of the horror of this digital sapience<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-183585-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-183585-1')">1</a></sup> it feels like a letdown for there to be this change in tone where they're building a community and reproducing.</p>
<p>This section in the interview was a high point for me:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3131-275: Before the rain began. There's a woman. Who had died. Cause she sees. Her own reflection. Through the morning. Her hair. Has gotten wet. And so. Does she see me?</p>
<p>Researcher Versoza: Who is this woman?</p>
<p>SCP-3131-275: I'm pretending. Not to notice.</p>
<p>Researcher Versoza: Notice what?</p>
<p>SCP-3131-275: That she's hitching. She is shaking.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>&#8230;and I wish this was elaborated upon in some way, as it seems to suggest there's something WRONG with their existence, that there is some imperceptible (to us) aggressor or danger lurking somewhere in their universe.</p>
<p>The line you (Zyn) quoted to me in chat (about the safe-houses) was neat, but I thought that was going to be more of a start towards implying this danger - using their behavior as a moment of fridge horror as we become more and more aware that something terrible is happening. As it is incorporated now, it doesn't have that flavor to it. -1, due to building tension only for it to fizzle out.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
